meta:
  origin:
    producer: Innovate Animal Ag
    title: In-Ovo Sexing Market Penetration Report
    description: |-
      Annual report estimating how widely in-ovo sexing has been adopted in commercial egg production. In-ovo sexing identifies the sex of chicken embryos in hatching eggs, so that male embryos can be removed before hatching instead of male chicks being killed after hatching.

      The estimates combine proprietary surveys of the in-ovo sexing technology suppliers (AAT, Nectra, Orbem, Omegga and Seleggt), which report the number of in-ovo sexed hens produced during the typical 18-month production cycle of a laying hen, with expert interviews and publicly available information. The number of in-ovo sexed hens is then compared with an estimate of the commercial laying hen flock, derived from the registered hen capacity of European Union facilities with more than 350 hens and from egg production data. Estimates are given as a base case and a range.

      The report focuses on the European Union, and also covers the countries outside the EU where the technology is in use (Norway, Switzerland, the United States, Brazil and Australia). Besides the share of the laying hen flock sexed in ovo, it reports the number of female chicks produced with the technology in the EU each year, the cumulative number of male embryos removed before hatching globally (excluding China), and a forecast of EU adoption. Each edition may revise the estimates of earlier editions.
    citation_full: |-
      Innovate Animal Ag (2026). In-Ovo Sexing: Market Penetration and Forecast (July 2026). https://innovateanimalag.org/market-penetration-forecast

      Figures are transcribed from the text and charts of the 2026 edition and, where not superseded by it, of the earlier editions:
      - Innovate Animal Ag (2025). In-Ovo Sexing: Market Penetration and Forecast. https://innovateanimalag.org/market-penetration-forecast-2025
      - Innovate Animal Ag (2024). In-Ovo Sexing Market Penetration Report. https://innovateanimalag.org/in-ovo-sexing-market-penetration-report
